# 3. Important Linux Directories

Some directories are particularly useful during security investigations.

### `/etc`

Contains system configuration files.

Examples:

```text
/etc/passwd
/etc/group
/etc/ssh/
/etc/systemd/
```

Unexpected changes in `/etc` can be important because configuration changes may affect authentication, services, or system behavior.

---

### `/var/log`

Contains many system and application logs.

```bash
ls -lah /var/log/
```

---

### `/usr/bin`

Contains many executable programs.

```bash
ls -lah /usr/bin/ | head
```

---

### `/tmp`

Used for temporary files.

```bash
ls -lah /tmp/
```

Unexpected executable files or scripts in temporary locations may deserve investigation.

