# 4. Why `/etc` Can Be Important

The `/etc` directory contains configuration files used by many Linux services.

Examples:

```text
/etc/passwd
/etc/group
/etc/ssh/
/etc/systemd/
/etc/cron.d/
```

A change to one of these files may affect:

* Users
* Groups
* Authentication
* SSH
* Services
* Scheduled tasks
* System configuration

Therefore, monitoring important files under `/etc` can be useful for security investigations.

