# 5. File Permissions

Linux permissions determine who can:

* Read
* Write
* Execute

Example:

```text
-rwxr-xr-x
```

The permissions are divided into:

```text
Owner | Group | Others
```

Example:

```text
rwx | r-x | r-x
```

Meaning:

```text
Owner  → read + write + execute
Group  → read + execute
Others → read + execute
```

---

# 6. Check File Permissions

Use:

```bash
ls -l /etc/passwd
```

Example:

```text
-rw-r--r-- 1 root root ... /etc/passwd
```

Important information:

```text
Permissions
Owner
Group
File
```

---

# 7. Check File Ownership

Use:

```bash
ls -l /etc/passwd
```

Or:

```bash
stat /etc/passwd
```

Example:

```text
Owner → root
Group → root
```

Unexpected ownership changes can be worth investigating.

