# 8. Using stat

`stat` provides detailed file metadata.

Example:

```bash
stat /etc/passwd
```

Important information includes:

```text
File
Size
Permissions
UID
GID
Access time
Modify time
Change time
```

This is useful during file investigations.

---

# 9. File Modification Time

Find the modification time:

```bash
stat /etc/passwd
```

Look for:

```text
Modify:
```

If a sensitive file was modified at an unusual time, investigate:

```text
Who changed it?
Why was it changed?
Was a package updated?
Was an administrator working?
```

