# 13. Checking File Changes with ls

View files with timestamps:

```bash
ls -lah /etc/
```

For a specific file:

```bash
ls -l /etc/passwd
```

Sort by modification time:

```bash
ls -lt /etc/
```

This can help identify recently modified files.

---

# 14. Finding Recently Modified Files

You can use `find`.

Example:

```bash
sudo find /etc -type f -mtime -1
```

This searches for files under `/etc` modified within approximately the last day.

Another example:

```bash
sudo find /etc -type f -mmin -60
```

This searches for files modified within approximately the last hour.

