# 🔍 23. Mini SOC Investigation

Suppose you discover:

```text
/etc/cron.d/update
```

First inspect it:

```bash
ls -l /etc/cron.d/update
```

Check metadata:

```bash
stat /etc/cron.d/update
```

Read it:

```bash
cat /etc/cron.d/update
```

Calculate its hash:

```bash
sha256sum /etc/cron.d/update
```

Then ask:

```text
Who created it?
When was it created?
What command does it execute?
Which user executes it?
Is the task expected?
Does the command launch a script?
Does the script make network connections?
```

Now correlate with previous lessons:

```text
Cron Job
   ↓
Script
   ↓
Process
   ↓
Network Connection
```

